# Dependencies and build output. Neither has ever been tracked in this repo -
# Railway installs and builds from source on every deploy - so ignoring them
# changes nothing about what ships. It just stops 280-odd packages and a dist/
# folder showing up as untracked noise in GitHub Desktop, where a bulk "commit
# everything" could sweep them in.
node_modules/
dist/

# Secrets. Nothing matching this is tracked today; keep it that way.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local logs
npm-debug.log*
*.log
